From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:56:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/27] prime: register gateways with LZT1 register v1/v2 and
 bind the payout by BIP322
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

POST /sovereignty/enrol (token, loopback) takes SOV-P-002 §4's messages. v1 is signed by G
over "XBT-SOVEREIGN-TIDES/register\0" ‖ message and names the gateway's node; v2 adds a
payout line and the payout owner's consent: BIP322 (simple or full), the legacy signmessage
for P2PKH (the pool node's verifymessage), or a confirmed spend from the payout to itself
carrying OP_RETURN "LZT1E" ‖ SHA256(message)[0..16]. at must be one of the pool node's last
144 blocks and move forward per key, so neither an old message nor one inside the window can
be replayed.

A v2's payout must match what Prime learned for the gateway (gateway-scripts.json), or else
its first split coinbase confirms it; paying elsewhere refuses the key. A new G from the same
payout supersedes the old one for good, its key age not carried; the payout can revoke its
binding (LZT1 revoke v2). Key age counts from the first v2's at block. Node addresses go to
sovereignty-nodes.json, 0600 from creation, and nowhere else. The old
"LZT1 register G=… pool=lazarus" ingest stays for the demos only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
